# ws/orm-semantics — safe, honest ORM materializer contract, A/B

This workstream changes only the consumer side: `fastpostgres.orm.materialize`
now proves a model is flat before using the native fill kernel, and returns
stock SQLAlchemy instances for any mapper shape the kernel cannot honor. The
native kernel (`native/materialize.cpp`) is unchanged; the transport is
unchanged. The benchmark script adds one cell, `materialize fallback`, that
prices the graceful fallback on a relationship model.

## Command

The same file is mounted into both images, so only the image tag and
`BENCH_GIT_REV` differ. Three alternating runs per image, `reps=5`, 100K rows,
`shape=bench` (short ASCII text, no NULLs).

```
flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
  -e BENCH_GIT_REV=<baseline|orm-semantics> \
  -v /home/carlos/.local/share/opencode/worktree/b2743c/ws-orm-semantics/bench/orm/materialize_bench.py:/src/bench/orm/materialize_bench.py:ro \
  fpq-<baseline|orm-semantics> \
  python3 /src/bench/orm/materialize_bench.py 100000 5'
```

